From 4371a50032e045ee4276e0c8c685973732671553 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:21:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] D10-D11: old-renderer shader fallback; the direct renderer is
 the default

D10: while the direct renderer's own translation of a draw's shaders, or its
pipeline, is not built yet, the draw uses the old renderer's stored
translations (its shader store, read only, Storage::DataBase::Legacy()). The
new translation is made on a worker and the new pipeline in the background;
draws switch over once they are ready. A key is made of new translations only or
of old ones only (forced), so old and new start bindings never mix. Pipelines of
old translations are built at once (the driver usually has them) and their keys
are not stored. Draws no longer wait for translations in progress when old
ones exist. Metas read from a store derive uses_direct from their buffers (the
byte was padding before D2). SHADGT_LEGACY_FALLBACK=0 turns it off.
Tokyo rain race with an empty direct store: 43.5 fps, 23 stalls >= 100 ms
(before: froze or ~27 fps; warm store ~43 fps, 12-27 stalls).

D11: the direct renderer is on unless SHADGT_DIRECT=0 (GPU.direct_renderer is
ignored).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
